# Perf-baseline Penca env template.
#
# Perf tests (`packages/penca/tests/performance/`) compare Penca against a
# direct Postgres baseline. For that comparison they open a plain psycopg
# connection to the same Postgres instance the `write` and `query` servicers
# use. These env vars — only `PENCA_DB_*` — drive that direct connection
# via `DbSettings`.
#
# Everything else the Penca write/read path touches (object storage,
# per-service knobs) stays inside the container network and is configured
# inline in `docker/compose.{python,rust}.yml`. There is no reason to leak
# those values to the host env.
#
# The Justfile generates `docker/.baseline.env` by sed-substituting
# __DB_PORT__ with the host port Docker bound for Postgres. Only the
# `perf-test` recipe sources this file; `integration-test` does not need it.
PENCA_DB_HOST=localhost
PENCA_DB_PORT=__DB_PORT__
PENCA_DB_DBNAME=penca
PENCA_DB_USER=penca
PENCA_DB_PASSWORD=penca
